msgid "Acknowledgement"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a Reactive Messaging Message associated with a RabbitMQ Message is "
"acknowledged, it informs the broker that the message has been _accepted_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether you need to explicitly acknowledge the message depends on the `auto-"
"acknowledgement` setting for the channel; if that is set to true then your "
"message will be automatically acknowledged on receipt."
msgstr ""

msgid "Failure Management"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a message produced from a RabbitMQ message is nacked, a failure strategy "
"is applied. The RabbitMQ connector supports\n"
"three strategies, controlled by the failure-strategy channel setting:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`fail` - fail the application; no more RabbitMQ messages will be processed. "
"The RabbitMQ message is marked as rejected."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`accept` - this strategy marks the RabbitMQ message as _accepted_. The "
"processing continues, ignoring the failure."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`reject` - this strategy marks the RabbitMQ message as rejected (default). "
"The processing continues with the next message."
msgstr ""

